Info-ZIP method fixtures (stuffr 0.16.0, Task 1)
================================================

Archives that the Info-ZIP decoder ports (stuffr_formats::infozip) are tested
against. Every file is at most 64 KiB, is committed byte-for-byte as fetched
(or generated as stated; lzma.zip is the one fetched file renamed, from .zipx), and
was checked with BOTH references:

  Apple   /usr/bin/unzip  (UnZip 6.00 of 20 April 2009, modified by Apple Inc.)
  Ubuntu  unzip 6.0-28ubuntu4.1 on ubuntu:24.04 (docker; zip 3.0-13ubuntu0.2)

Both exit 0 on `unzip -t` for every supported fixture. The unsupported ones
(aes*, lzma, and bzip2 on Apple) are listed at the bottom with each
reference's exact exit code and message.

Sources and licences
--------------------
Licence texts are in LICENSES/: Apache-2.0.txt and commons-compress-NOTICE.txt
(commons-compress, same commit), zip2-MIT.txt (zip2, same commit),
libarchive-BSD-2-Clause.txt (libarchive COPYING at v3.7.7).
Excluded from the published crate (`exclude` in Cargo.toml); tests read these
files at run time from CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR.

 libarchive v3.7.7        https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive/tree/v3.7.7
                          libarchive/test/<name>.uu, decoded with uudecode.
                          BSD-2-Clause.
 commons-compress         https://github.com/apache/commons-compress
                          commit 611cad06b66842692870c6ae98f50de7ce4f25d5,
                          src/test/resources/<name>. Apache-2.0.
 zip2 (zip-rs)            https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2
                          commit 15639ba675933ab79f1aa425f21ebd0cf3ed482f,
                          tests/data/<name>. MIT.

